#!/bin/sh
# Process-tree RSS cap policy for a parallel compiler build.
#
# Why this exists: the cap was a fixed 5859375 KiB (6 GB) with a fixed
# hard ceiling, regardless of worker count (6835937 KiB / 7 GB until
# 2026-10-12, when measured compiler peaks widened it to 8388608 KiB /
# 8 GiB; then 2026-10-13 measured stage2 full-CLI AOT peaks of 6842388 KiB
# widened it to 10485760 KiB / 10 GiB and finally 16777216 KiB / 16 GiB —
# see BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_STATIC_CEILING_KIB below). The tree's real
# peak grows with --threads because every worker holds one in-flight module.
# Measured on the seed->stage2 native build (Windows Job Object; sum of member
# working sets / peak job commit):
#     19 jobs  2.85 GiB / 3.21 GiB
#     40 jobs  4.03-4.41 GiB / 4.61-4.77 GiB
#     80 jobs  killed at the 5.59 GiB cap (exit 88) while still growing
# i.e. about 1.4-1.8 GiB of fixed cost plus 57-76 MiB per worker. Commit is above
# the working-set sum, so the reading is real memory, not double counting.
#
# Those are CODEGEN workers, and that pricing (96 MiB/job) is the Windows
# default, where the frontend is pinned to one worker by policy. On every other
# host a native-build with --threads N also fans out N HIR shard workers
# (measured 2.4-3.3 GB RSS each, src/app/cli/shard_mem_clamp.spl), and the
# compiler admits them from the enforced cap: workers = cap * 60% / 3000000 KiB.
# A job is therefore priced at 3000000 / 0.6 ~= 5120 MiB there; the 96 MiB
# pricing pinned every cap at the 5.59 GiB floor, i.e. one HIR worker at any
# thread count (bug bootstrap_frontend_budget_pins_one_hir_worker_2026-10-19).
# Keep the three constants (worker budget, 60%, per-job price) in step.
#
# Budget (tunable, host config `tree_rss_*`, see config/host/host_config.sdn):
#     cap = max(BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_FLOOR_KIB,
#               (base_mib + jobs * per_job_mib) * 1024)
#     cap = min(cap, host_total_kib * host_pct / 100)   when host RAM is known
#     cap = min(cap, hard ceiling)
# Default hard ceiling (process-tree-rss-watchdog.pl recomputes the same
# value from --compiler-jobs and refuses anything above it):
#     ceiling = max(25165824, min(3145728 + jobs * 1048576, host_total_kib * 3/4))
# With no worker count, or with host RAM unreadable, the ceiling stays at the
# historical 6835937 KiB, widened on positive evidence: 8388608 KiB on
# 2026-10-12 measured compiler peaks, then 16777216 KiB on 2026-10-13
# stage2 full-CLI receipts (the watchdog receipt for the same constant
# carries the measurement).
# Explicit SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB is a separate compiler-only
# opt-in, admitted by both owners under 75% of fresh real total AND available
# memory. It requires enforced scope, declared workers and an explicit cap.
#
# Precedence per knob: SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_<KNOB> > SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_
# <KNOB> / host config (scripts/setup/host-env.shs --get) > built-in default.
# An explicit SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB replaces the formula
# but is REFUSED (never clamped) above the hard ceiling, with the reason in
# bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal.
#
# Result attribution: bootstrap_tree_rss_source says which layer chose the
# numbers (explicit-env | env-knobs | host-config | default) and
# bootstrap_tree_rss_bound which rule produced the final value (explicit |
# budget | floor | host-fraction | hard-ceiling). Callers pass both to the
# watchdog (--cap-source / --cap-bound) so the receipt records them.
#
# Test hook: BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH substitutes host RAM, which can
# raise the ceiling. It is honoured only with BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE=1
# AND SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE=monitor; set any other way it is a
# refusal, never ignored. bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source records
# proc-meminfo | sysctl | fixture | unknown.
#
# Source it, or run:  tree-rss-policy.shs --resolve JOBS [REPO_ROOT]
#                     tree-rss-policy.shs --selftest

BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_FLOOR_KIB=5859375
# Widened 2026-10-13 on positive evidence: stage2 full-CLI artifact builds
# (mcp/compiler_cli/test_runner/lsp closures, AOT emission at threads=4)
# measured peak_rss_kib=6842388 (watchdog receipt, stage2-compiler-tests
# campaign 2026-10-12/13, cycles 19/20/21/23 — each killed at the old
# 6835937 ceiling after MIR, during codegen). 8 GiB hosts ~1.2 GiB headroom
# over the measured peak on a 127 GiB host. Keep in sync with
# scripts/resource/process-tree-rss-watchdog.pl (it recomputes and refuses
# anything above).
# Second widening 2026-10-13: compiler_cli (largest closure) still
# exceeded 8 GiB at 2 threads (watchdog receipts: 6842388 -> 8411200 ->
# >8388608 across cycles 23/24/25). 10 GiB is the new ceiling; the
# treadmill is logged in doc/08_tracking/bug/stage2_full_cli_artifact_layer
# _2026-10-12.md. Keep in sync with process-tree-rss-watchdog.pl.
# Third widening 2026-10-13: compiler_cli (2546-module closure) exceeded
# 10 GiB at 2 build threads with group-scoping in effect (per-task receipt
# peak_rss_kib=10504072 at 73% HIR; kill at cap, cycle 31). 12 GiB. Keep in
# sync with process-tree-rss-watchdog.pl.
# Fourth widening 2026-10-13: compiler_cli exceeds 12 GiB even at 1 build
# thread (per-task group-scoped receipt peak 12591996 KiB, cycle 33) — the
# footprint is the compiler's own working set over the 2546-module closure,
# not shard workers. 16 GiB on a 127 GiB host, one build at a time. Keep in
# sync with process-tree-rss-watchdog.pl.
# Fifth widening 2026-10-16: cycle-44 peak 16792808 KiB (8 compiler jobs) and
# cycle-46 peak 16777468 KiB (4 jobs) — both killed by the watchdog at the
# 16 GiB ceiling. The plateau is baseline-dominated (resident compiler daemon
# + shared LLVM over the SCV closure), so job reduction cannot fit 16 GiB.
# 24 GiB leaves ~7 GiB headroom over the measured plateau. Keep in sync with
# process-tree-rss-watchdog.pl.
# Sixth widening 2026-10-16: cycle 49 serialized probe -- a single cli
# closure build exceeds 24 GiB on the merged tree; 48 GiB measures the true
# plateau before final tightening. Keep in sync with process-tree-rss-watchdog.pl.
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_STATIC_CEILING_KIB=50331648
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_RESERVE_KIB=3145728
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_CEILING_KIB=1048576
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_BASE_MIB_DEFAULT=3072
# Per-job price: one 3000000 KiB HIR shard worker admitted at 60% of the cap
# on fanout hosts; a 57-76 MiB codegen shard where the frontend is pinned.
case "$(uname -s 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)" in
  MSYS*|MINGW*|CYGWIN*) BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB_DEFAULT=96 ;;
  *) BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB_DEFAULT=5120 ;;
esac
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT_DEFAULT=50
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT_MAX=75
# Host-scaled default (2026-10-25). When the job-priced budget is below the
# need (bound floor or budget; Windows 96 MiB/job pricing: 27 workers = 5.59 GiB on a 128 GB host),
# the cap is raised to what the workers really need, (base + jobs * worker_mem)
# with worker_mem from SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_WORKER_MEM_MIB > SIMPLE_HOST_WORKER_MEM_MIB
# > host config worker_mem_mib (the same knob that sizes the job count) > 3300,
# bounded by this share of host RAM and then by the hard ceiling. Unknown host
# RAM keeps the floor. Any tree_rss_* knob or explicit cap bypasses it.
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_SCALE_PCT=60
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_WORKER_MEM_MIB_DEFAULT=3300

# Whole-build phase pricing (Stage 2 compiler tests, 2026-11-05). The phase
# runs full-CLI closure builds whose WORKERS (pool HIR shard workers, or the
# single in-process build when the pool is skipped) each need this FLOOR, KiB.
# Measured:
#   2026-11-05, 121 GiB aarch64 Linux host (MemTotal 127600812 KiB),
#     release/1.0.0 0ff9a746185, cranelift, build-threads=8: three HIR shard
#     workers (admission estimate 9,000,000 kB each) all finished load_sources
#     (4437 files) at ~15.6 GiB EACH and the tree was killed at the 48 GiB cap
#     before HIR began (peak_rss_kib=50366440, exit 88).
#   2026-11-05, same host, build-threads=1 (in-process, no pool): the campaign
#     cap sat at 5859375 KiB and the build was killed at HIR module 9/3005
#     (peak_rss_kib=5860212) -- the compile-shard floor is below ONE worker.
#   2026-10-13, x86_64 Windows, 2546-module closure, 1 thread (cycle 33):
#     per-task peak 12591996 KiB at 73% HIR; cycles 44/46 (8 and 4 jobs):
#     16.0 GiB plateau, killed at the then 16 GiB ceiling.
# 15.6 GiB is load_sources ALONE and HIR grows on top of it, so 16 GiB is a
# floor, never a cap: the cap is base + workers x floor x margin, and the
# worker count is reduced to what the host budget holds at that price
# (bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_plan) instead of capping below the floor.
# A worker measured above floor x margin is evidence to raise the FLOOR here
# (and in the bug record), not to widen the margin.
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB=16777216
# Immutable defaults the env-resolution compares against, so repeated
# resolutions in one shell stay anchored to the shipped policy.
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_DEFAULT_KIB=$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB
# Runaway margin over the floor, percent of the floor: a tree above
# base + workers x floor x margin is a genuine runaway and is still killed
# (exit 88); HIR growth over the post-load_sources floor stays admitted.
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_PCT=150
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_DEFAULT_PCT=$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_PCT
# Non-worker residue of the phase tree: build coordinator (measured 1.32 GiB,
# 2026-10-27), verifier shell, campaign watchdog, interpreter test workers
# (they run already-built binaries spec by spec; unmeasured, small).
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB=4194304
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_DEFAULT_KIB=$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB
# Upper bound on the whole-build phase timeout scale. The time budgets
# (native internal 1800 s, row 3600 s, campaign 7200 s) were calibrated for the
# REQUESTED worker count; when the plan fits fewer workers the same module
# count takes proportionally longer, so the defaults are scaled by
# ceil(requested / fitted), bounded here so nothing becomes unbounded.
# Measured 2026-11-05 (bootstrap run 4, release/1.0.0 13a060d644e, 121 GiB
# aarch64): 8 requested -> 2 fitted; both MIR shard workers were killed at the
# 1800 s internal timeout with 596 of 3010 modules claimed (~0.68 modules/s
# combined after ~900 s of pre-MIR setup), i.e. ~75 min of MIR alone. x4 gives
# 7200 s internal / 14400 s row / 28800 s campaign; a hung worker is still
# killed at the scaled limit.
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TIMEOUT_SCALE_MAX=4
# compiler_cli_build ROW cap of the whole-build phase, KiB (60 GiB; owner
# decision 2026-11-06). Applies to that one row only, and only when the plan
# runs >= 2 workers, the plan cap is below it and the host budget holds it;
# otherwise the row keeps the plan cap (bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_plan).
# Measured, run 11 (2026-11-06, release/1.0.0 e4c8830efc7, Stage 2 binary
# sha256 7daae128..., 121 GiB aarch64, host budget 63800400 KiB): with
# SIMPLE_MIR_SHARD_COUNT=8 the row was killed at the 54525952 KiB plan cap
# (rss-cap-exceeded, peak_rss_kib=54579388) in native_compile of MIR shard 1
# (20/382): two MIR shard workers sampled at 24.0 and 25.2 GiB plus a
# ~1.1 GiB coordinator; host MemAvailable never fell below 35 GiB. Why a row
# cap and not a higher worker FLOOR: the floor was measured for HIR
# load_sources and prices every full-CLI row; raising it would also re-price
# test_runner_build and the other rows, which did not exceed the plan. 60 GiB
# leaves ~8.5 GiB over the measured 2 x 25.2 + 1.1 GiB. The rows run SERIALLY
# here (BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TOOL_BUILD_CONCURRENCY=1 in bootstrap-from-scratch.sh),
# so the campaign envelope is the largest row cap, not a sum
# (bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_envelope). Record:
# doc/08_tracking/bug/stage2_compiler_cli_build_mir_shard_share_unbounded_2026-11-06.md
BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB=62914560

# bootstrap_tree_rss_worker_mem_mib REPO_ROOT -> per-worker MiB (always valid).
bootstrap_tree_rss_worker_mem_mib() {
  btr_wm=${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_WORKER_MEM_MIB:-${SIMPLE_HOST_WORKER_MEM_MIB:-}}
  if [ -z "$btr_wm" ] && [ -n "${1:-}" ] && [ -f "$1/scripts/setup/host-env.shs" ]; then
    btr_wm=$(sh "$1/scripts/setup/host-env.shs" --get worker_mem_mib 2>/dev/null | tail -n 1) || btr_wm=
  fi
  bootstrap_tree_rss_is_uint "$btr_wm" 7 || btr_wm=$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_WORKER_MEM_MIB_DEFAULT
  printf '%s\n' "$btr_wm"
}

# bootstrap_tree_rss_workers_fit CAP_KIB WORKER_MEM_MIB [BASE_MIB] -> workers
# the cap can hold (>= 1).
bootstrap_tree_rss_workers_fit() {
  btr_wf=$(( ($1 / 1024 - ${3:-$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_BASE_MIB_DEFAULT}) / $2 ))
  [ "$btr_wf" -ge 1 ] || btr_wf=1
  printf '%s\n' "$btr_wf"
}

# Decimal, non-zero, at most $2 digits (bounded so $(( )) cannot overflow).
bootstrap_tree_rss_is_uint() {
  case "$1" in ''|*[!0-9]*) return 1 ;; esac
  [ "${#1}" -le "$2" ] || return 1
  case "$1" in *[1-9]*) return 0 ;; *) return 1 ;; esac
}

# Canonical decimal for a small count: strips leading zeros so 08/09 cannot
# crash $(( )) and 040 cannot be read as octal 32. Prints nothing for junk
# (non-digits, empty, more than $2 significant digits).
bootstrap_tree_rss_canonical_uint() {
  case "$1" in ''|*[!0-9]*) return 0 ;; esac
  btr_cu=$1
  while :; do
    case "$btr_cu" in 0?*) btr_cu=${btr_cu#0} ;; *) break ;; esac
  done
  [ "${#btr_cu}" -le "$2" ] || return 0
  printf '%s\n' "$btr_cu"
}

# MemTotal (KiB) of one meminfo-format file, or empty.
bootstrap_tree_rss_meminfo_total() {
  btr_mt=
  [ ! -r "$1" ] || btr_mt=$(awk '/^MemTotal:/ { print $2; exit }' "$1" 2>/dev/null) || btr_mt=
  bootstrap_tree_rss_is_uint "$btr_mt" 15 || btr_mt=
  printf '%s\n' "$btr_mt"
}

# MemAvailable (KiB; MemFree when the kernel has no MemAvailable) of one
# meminfo-format file, or empty. Only ever LOWERS a budget (whole-build plan),
# so an absent line is "no headroom evidence", never a wider budget.
bootstrap_tree_rss_meminfo_available() {
  btr_ma=
  [ ! -r "$1" ] || btr_ma=$(awk '
    /^MemAvailable:/ { avail=$2 }
    /^MemFree:/ { free=$2 }
    END { if (avail != "") print avail; else if (free != "") print free }' "$1" 2>/dev/null) || btr_ma=
  bootstrap_tree_rss_is_uint "$btr_ma" 15 || btr_ma=
  printf '%s\n' "$btr_ma"
}

# Sets bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib (may be empty),
# bootstrap_tree_rss_host_available_kib (may be empty; never from sysctl) and
# bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source. Returns 1 with a refusal when the
# test fixture hook is present without its switch or while the cap is enforced.
bootstrap_tree_rss_probe_host() {
  bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib=
  bootstrap_tree_rss_host_available_kib=
  if [ -n "${BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH+x}" ]; then
    bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source=fixture
    [ "${BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE:-}" = 1 ] || {
      bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal='tree RSS policy: BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH is a test-only host memory fixture and requires BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE=1'
      return 1
    }
    [ "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE:-enforce}" = monitor ] || {
      bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal='tree RSS policy: a host memory fixture is refused while the RSS cap is enforced (SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE=monitor is required)'
      return 1
    }
    bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_meminfo_total "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH")
    bootstrap_tree_rss_host_available_kib=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_meminfo_available "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH")
    return 0
  fi
  bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_meminfo_total /proc/meminfo)
  bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source=proc-meminfo
  [ -z "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib" ] || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_host_available_kib=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_meminfo_available /proc/meminfo)
    return 0
  }
  for btr_sysctl in hw.memsize hw.physmem; do
    btr_bytes=$(sysctl -n "$btr_sysctl" 2>/dev/null) || btr_bytes=
    if bootstrap_tree_rss_is_uint "$btr_bytes" 18; then
      bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib=$((btr_bytes / 1024))
      bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source=sysctl
      return 0
    fi
  done
  bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source=unknown
}

# bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib JOBS HOST_TOTAL_KIB -> hard ceiling. JOBS 0
# (undeclared) or an empty HOST_TOTAL_KIB yields the static ceiling.
bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib() {
  btr_c_jobs=$1
  btr_c_host=$2
  btr_c=$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_STATIC_CEILING_KIB
  if bootstrap_tree_rss_is_uint "$btr_c_jobs" 3 && [ "$btr_c_jobs" -le 128 ] &&
     bootstrap_tree_rss_is_uint "$btr_c_host" 15; then
    btr_c_scaled=$((BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_RESERVE_KIB + btr_c_jobs * BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_CEILING_KIB))
    btr_c_host_max=$((btr_c_host / 4 * 3))
    [ "$btr_c_scaled" -le "$btr_c_host_max" ] || btr_c_scaled=$btr_c_host_max
    [ "$btr_c_scaled" -le "$btr_c" ] || btr_c=$btr_c_scaled
  fi
  printf '%s\n' "$btr_c"
}

# Strict facts for an explicit elevated budget. This parser is also exercised
# with inert text fixtures; admission itself always reads the real /proc file.
bootstrap_tree_rss_headroom_facts() {
  awk '
    /^Mem(Total|Available|Free):/ {
      key=$1
      if (++seen[key] != 1 || NF != 3 || $3 != "kB" ||
          $2 !~ /^[1-9][0-9]*$/ || length($2) > 15) bad=1
      value[key]=$2
    }
    END {
      source=seen["MemAvailable:"] ? "MemAvailable:" : "MemFree:"
      total=value["MemTotal:"]; available=value[source]
      if (bad || seen["MemTotal:"] != 1 || seen[source] != 1 ||
          available+0 > total+0 || available+0 <= 0 || total+0 <= 0 ||
          (seen["MemFree:"] && value["MemFree:"]+0 > total+0)) exit 1
      printf "%s %s %s\n", total, available, source
    }' "$1"
}

bootstrap_tree_rss_admit_ceiling() {
  bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_request_kib=0
  bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_previous_kib=$bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib
  bootstrap_tree_rss_available_kib=0
  bootstrap_tree_rss_available_source=unknown
  bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_admission=default
  [ -n "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB+x}" ] || return 0
  bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_admission=refused
  btr_requested=$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB
  case "$btr_requested" in ''|0*|*[!0-9]*)
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal='tree RSS policy: compiler ceiling must be canonical positive decimal'; return 1 ;;
  esac
  [ "${#btr_requested}" -le 15 ] || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal='tree RSS policy: compiler ceiling is oversized'; return 1;
  }
  bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_request_kib=$btr_requested
  case "$btr_explicit" in ''|0*|*[!0-9]*)
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal='tree RSS policy: elevated ceiling requires an explicit canonical positive cap'; return 1 ;;
  esac
  [ "${#btr_explicit}" -le 15 ] && [ "$btr_jobs" -gt 0 ] &&
    [ "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE:-enforce}" = enforce ] &&
    [ -z "${BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH+x}" ] &&
    [ -z "${BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE+x}" ] &&
    [ -z "${SIMPLE_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH+x}" ] &&
    [ -z "${SIMPLE_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE+x}" ] || {
      bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal='tree RSS policy: elevated ceiling requires real host memory, explicit workers and enforced compiler scope'; return 1;
    }
  btr_facts=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_headroom_facts /proc/meminfo) || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal='tree RSS policy: real host headroom is unavailable or contradictory'; return 1;
  }
  read -r bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib bootstrap_tree_rss_available_kib bootstrap_tree_rss_available_source <<EOF
$btr_facts
EOF
  bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source=proc-meminfo
  btr_total_bound=$((bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib / 4 * 3))
  btr_available_bound=$((bootstrap_tree_rss_available_kib / 4 * 3))
  [ "$btr_requested" -gt "$bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_previous_kib" ] &&
    [ "$btr_requested" -le "$btr_total_bound" ] &&
    [ "$btr_requested" -le "$btr_available_bound" ] &&
    [ "$btr_explicit" -le "$btr_requested" ] || {
      bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: compiler ceiling $btr_requested refused (previous=$bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_previous_kib total_bound=$btr_total_bound available_bound=$btr_available_bound cap=$btr_explicit)"; return 1;
    }
  bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib=$btr_requested
  bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_admission=elevated
}

bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_metadata() {
  printf 'compiler_ceiling_request_kib=%s\ncompiler_ceiling_previous_kib=%s\ncompiler_ceiling_admitted_kib=%s\ncompiler_available_kib=%s\ncompiler_available_source=%s\ncompiler_ceiling_admission=%s\n' \
    "${bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_request_kib:-0}" "${bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_previous_kib:-0}" \
    "$(if [ "${bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_admission:-refused}" = refused ]; then printf 0; else printf '%s' "${bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib:-0}"; fi)" \
    "${bootstrap_tree_rss_available_kib:-0}" "${bootstrap_tree_rss_available_source:-unknown}" \
    "${bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_admission:-refused}"
}

# One knob: specific env > SIMPLE_HOST_* env > host config file > default.
# An invalid value at any layer is a refusal, not a silent fallback: a typo in
# a memory budget must not quietly become a different budget.
bootstrap_tree_rss_knob() {
  btr_k_name=$1 btr_k_key=$2 btr_k_default=$3 btr_k_digits=$4 btr_k_root=$5
  eval "btr_k_value=\${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_${btr_k_name}:-}"
  btr_k_source=env
  if [ -z "$btr_k_value" ]; then
    eval "btr_k_value=\${SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_${btr_k_name}:-}"
    btr_k_source=host-env
  fi
  if [ -z "$btr_k_value" ] && [ -n "$btr_k_root" ] &&
     [ -f "$btr_k_root/scripts/setup/host-env.shs" ]; then
    # host-env.shs warns on stderr and falls through to a lower layer when a
    # config FILE value is invalid. For a memory budget that fall-through is
    # exactly the silent substitution this function refuses, so read the
    # warning instead of discarding it.
    btr_k_out=$(sh "$btr_k_root/scripts/setup/host-env.shs" --get "$btr_k_key" 2>&1) || btr_k_out=
    btr_k_warning=$(printf '%s\n' "$btr_k_out" | grep "^host-config: warning: ignoring invalid $btr_k_key=" | head -n 1) || btr_k_warning=
    [ -z "$btr_k_warning" ] || {
      bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: invalid $btr_k_key in host config (${btr_k_warning#host-config: warning: })"
      return 1
    }
    btr_k_value=$(printf '%s\n' "$btr_k_out" | grep -v '^host-config: warning:' | tail -n 1) || btr_k_value=
    btr_k_source=host-config
  fi
  if [ -z "$btr_k_value" ]; then
    btr_k_value=$btr_k_default
    btr_k_source=default
  fi
  bootstrap_tree_rss_is_uint "$btr_k_value" "$btr_k_digits" || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: invalid $btr_k_key=$btr_k_value (source: $btr_k_source)"
    return 1
  }
  # Weakest-to-strongest attribution across the three knobs.
  case "$btr_k_source:$bootstrap_tree_rss_source" in
    env:*|host-env:*) bootstrap_tree_rss_source=env-knobs ;;
    host-config:default) bootstrap_tree_rss_source=host-config ;;
  esac
}

# Receipt attribution spelling the watchdog accepts (it dies on anything else).
bootstrap_tree_rss_attribution_valid() {
  case "$1" in ''|[!a-z]*|*[!a-z-]*) return 1 ;; esac
  [ "${#1}" -le 32 ]
}

# A cap the whole-build phase policy published arrives at every owner as the
# same env var a user-set diagnostic pair uses, so by itself it would be
# attributed explicit-env/explicit everywhere (campaign AND build rows), and
# an admitted phase-policy elevation would be indistinguishable from a
# diagnostic attempt. The publisher also sets
# SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE/_BOUND; when both are present
# they replace the explicit-env attribution in every owner's receipt. A
# diagnostic pair (no attribution vars) stays explicit-env. A malformed
# spelling is a refusal, never laundered to another label.
bootstrap_tree_rss_published_attribution() {
  [ -n "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE+x}${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND+x}" ] || return 0
  bootstrap_tree_rss_attribution_valid "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE:-}" &&
    bootstrap_tree_rss_attribution_valid "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND:-}" || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: invalid published cap attribution SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE='${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE:-}' _BOUND='${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND:-}' (want [a-z][a-z-]{0,31}, both set)"
    return 1
  }
  bootstrap_tree_rss_source=$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE
  bootstrap_tree_rss_bound=$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND
}

# bootstrap_tree_rss_resolve JOBS [REPO_ROOT]
# Sets bootstrap_tree_rss_{cap_kib,ceiling_kib,host_total_kib,
# host_total_source,source,bound,summary}.
# Returns 1 with bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal set when the request is refused.
bootstrap_tree_rss_resolve() {
  btr_jobs=${1:-0}
  btr_root=${2:-}
  bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal=
  # A failure before the host probe must not publish a previous invocation's
  # successful admission metadata when this sourced owner is called again.
  bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_request_kib=0
  bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_previous_kib=0
  bootstrap_tree_rss_available_kib=0
  bootstrap_tree_rss_available_source=unknown
  bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_admission=refused
  if [ -n "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB+x}" ]; then
    case "$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB" in ''|0*|*[!0-9]*) ;;
      *) [ "${#SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB}" -gt 15 ] ||
           bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_request_kib=$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB ;;
    esac
  fi
  btr_jobs=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_canonical_uint "$btr_jobs" 3)
  [ -n "$btr_jobs" ] && [ "$btr_jobs" -le 128 ] || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: worker count must be a decimal 0..128, got '${1:-}'"
    return 1
  }
  bootstrap_tree_rss_probe_host || return 1
  bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib "$btr_jobs" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib")
  btr_explicit=${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB:-}
  bootstrap_tree_rss_admit_ceiling || return 1
  if [ -n "$btr_explicit" ]; then
    bootstrap_tree_rss_is_uint "$btr_explicit" 15 || {
      bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: invalid SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=$btr_explicit"
      return 1
    }
    [ "$btr_explicit" -le "$bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib" ] || {
      bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=$btr_explicit KiB exceeds the hard ceiling $bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib KiB for $btr_jobs worker(s) (host RAM ${bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib:-unknown} KiB via ${bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source}; ceiling = max($BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_STATIC_CEILING_KIB, min($BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_RESERVE_KIB + jobs*$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_CEILING_KIB, 3/4 host RAM)))"
      return 1
    }
    bootstrap_tree_rss_cap_kib=$btr_explicit
    bootstrap_tree_rss_source=explicit-env
    bootstrap_tree_rss_bound=explicit
    bootstrap_tree_rss_published_attribution || return 1
  else
    bootstrap_tree_rss_source=default
    bootstrap_tree_rss_knob BASE_MIB tree_rss_base_mib "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_BASE_MIB_DEFAULT" 7 "$btr_root" || return 1
    btr_base=$btr_k_value
    bootstrap_tree_rss_knob PER_JOB_MIB tree_rss_per_job_mib "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB_DEFAULT" 6 "$btr_root" || return 1
    btr_per_job=$btr_k_value
    bootstrap_tree_rss_knob HOST_PCT tree_rss_host_pct "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT_DEFAULT" 2 "$btr_root" || return 1
    btr_pct=$btr_k_value
    [ "$btr_pct" -le "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT_MAX" ] || {
      bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: tree_rss_host_pct=$btr_pct exceeds $BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT_MAX"
      return 1
    }
    btr_cap=$(((btr_base + btr_jobs * btr_per_job) * 1024))
    bootstrap_tree_rss_bound=budget
    if [ "$btr_jobs" -eq 0 ] || [ "$btr_cap" -lt "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_FLOOR_KIB" ]; then
      btr_cap=$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_FLOOR_KIB
      bootstrap_tree_rss_bound=floor
    fi
    if [ -n "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib" ]; then
      btr_host_cap=$((bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib / 100 * btr_pct))
      if [ "$btr_cap" -gt "$btr_host_cap" ] && [ "$btr_cap" -gt "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_FLOOR_KIB" ]; then
        btr_cap=$btr_host_cap
        [ "$btr_cap" -ge "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_FLOOR_KIB" ] || btr_cap=$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_FLOOR_KIB
        bootstrap_tree_rss_bound=host-fraction
      fi
    fi
    if { [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_bound" = floor ] || [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_bound" = budget ]; } && [ "$btr_jobs" -gt 0 ] &&
       [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_source" = default ] && [ -n "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib" ]; then
      btr_wm=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_worker_mem_mib "$btr_root")
      btr_scaled=$(((btr_base + btr_jobs * btr_wm) * 1024))
      btr_scale_cap=$((bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib / 100 * BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_SCALE_PCT))
      [ "$btr_scaled" -le "$btr_scale_cap" ] || btr_scaled=$btr_scale_cap
      if [ "$btr_scaled" -gt "$btr_cap" ]; then
        btr_cap=$btr_scaled
        bootstrap_tree_rss_bound=host-scaled
      fi
    fi
    if [ "$btr_cap" -gt "$bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib" ]; then
      btr_cap=$bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib
      bootstrap_tree_rss_bound=hard-ceiling
    fi
    bootstrap_tree_rss_cap_kib=$btr_cap
  fi
  bootstrap_tree_rss_summary="cap ${bootstrap_tree_rss_cap_kib} KiB (source: ${bootstrap_tree_rss_source}, bound: ${bootstrap_tree_rss_bound}, workers: ${btr_jobs}, hard ceiling: ${bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib} KiB, host RAM: ${bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib:-unknown} KiB via ${bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source}; compiler ceiling admission: ${bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_admission}, requested: ${bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_request_kib}, previous: ${bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_previous_kib}, available: $(if [ "${bootstrap_tree_rss_available_source}" = unknown ]; then printf unknown; else printf '%s KiB' "${bootstrap_tree_rss_available_kib}"; fi) via ${bootstrap_tree_rss_available_source})"
}

# Cap for a phase that wraps whole compiler builds (Stage 2 compiler tests:
# full-CLI + test-runner tool builds plus test workers). The compile-worker
# budget (base + jobs*96 MiB) prices a worker at a compile-shard's ~60-76 MiB,
# so for this phase it always falls to the 5.59 GiB floor, while the full-CLI
# build alone was measured above 12 GiB (see the ceiling widenings above):
# the default lane could never pass on a large host (exit 88, doc/08_tracking/
# bug/tree_rss_floor_kills_stage2_compiler_tests_on_large_hosts_2026-10-15.md).
# Price the phase by the host instead: host_pct of RAM, clamped to
# [floor, jobs-scaled ceiling]. Small hosts keep the host-fraction bound.
# Call after bootstrap_tree_rss_resolve JOBS; prints KiB.
bootstrap_tree_rss_phase_cap_kib() {
  btr_pc=$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_FLOOR_KIB
  if [ -n "${bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib:-}" ]; then
    bootstrap_tree_rss_knob HOST_PCT tree_rss_host_pct "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT_DEFAULT" 2 "${1:-}" || return 1
    btr_pc=$((bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib / 100 * btr_k_value))
    [ "$btr_pc" -ge "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_FLOOR_KIB" ] || btr_pc=$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_FLOOR_KIB
  fi
  [ "$btr_pc" -le "$bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib" ] || btr_pc=$bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib
  printf '%s\n' "$btr_pc"
}

# Per-worker reservation of the whole-build phase: floor x margin, KiB.
bootstrap_tree_rss_phase_worker_kib() {
  printf '%s\n' $((BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB * BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_PCT / 100))
}

# bootstrap_tree_rss_timeout_scale REQUESTED FITTED -> min(ceil(R/F), MAX), >= 1.
# Anything that is not a positive decimal pair (or F >= R) scales by 1.
bootstrap_tree_rss_timeout_scale() {
  btr_ts_r=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_canonical_uint "${1:-}" 3)
  btr_ts_w=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_canonical_uint "${2:-}" 3)
  btr_ts=1
  if [ -n "$btr_ts_r" ] && [ -n "$btr_ts_w" ] && [ "$btr_ts_w" -ge 1 ] && [ "$btr_ts_r" -gt "$btr_ts_w" ]; then
    btr_ts=$(((btr_ts_r + btr_ts_w - 1) / btr_ts_w))
    [ "$btr_ts" -le "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TIMEOUT_SCALE_MAX" ] || btr_ts=$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TIMEOUT_SCALE_MAX
  fi
  printf '%s\n' "$btr_ts"
}

# bootstrap_tree_rss_scaled_timeout VAR DEFAULT_SECONDS
# Publishes the whole-build phase time budget VAR (an env var name): an
# explicit, user-set non-empty VAR is honoured verbatim (it must still be a
# positive decimal; the verifier's own policy refuses anything else); else
# DEFAULT x bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_timeout_scale. Exports VAR and folds the
# attribution into BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SOURCE (explicit | phase-policy |
# phase-policy-scaled, comma-joined VAR:source) and BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SCALE
# for the verification receipt. Returns 1 on a malformed DEFAULT.
bootstrap_tree_rss_scaled_timeout() {
  btr_sto_var=$1
  btr_sto_default=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_canonical_uint "${2:-}" 6)
  [ -n "$btr_sto_default" ] && [ "$btr_sto_default" -gt 0 ] || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: default timeout for $btr_sto_var must be a positive decimal, got '${2:-}'"
    return 1
  }
  case "$btr_sto_var" in ''|*[!A-Z0-9_]*) bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: bad timeout variable '$btr_sto_var'"; return 1 ;; esac
  eval "btr_sto_explicit=\${$btr_sto_var:-}"
  btr_sto_scale=${bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_timeout_scale:-1}
  if [ -n "$btr_sto_explicit" ]; then
    btr_sto_source=explicit
  else
    eval "$btr_sto_var=\$((btr_sto_default * btr_sto_scale))"
    btr_sto_source=phase-policy
    [ "$btr_sto_scale" -le 1 ] || btr_sto_source=phase-policy-scaled
  fi
  export "$btr_sto_var"
  BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SOURCE="${BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SOURCE:+$BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SOURCE,}$btr_sto_var:$btr_sto_source"
  BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SCALE=$btr_sto_scale
  export BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SOURCE BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SCALE
}
# Apply lane-local overrides of the whole-build phase worker pricing
# (SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB / _MARGIN_PCT / _BASE_KIB).
# Defaults price a COLD full-CLI build and stay the small-host protection;
# warm-cache lanes and larger hosts may LOWER them, never raise them (raising
# the floor or margin is a policy change, not a lane tuning, and a typo must
# not silently buy a bigger reservation than admission would grant).
# Returns 1 with bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal on a malformed or raising value.
bootstrap_tree_rss_phase_pricing_resolve() {
  case ${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB:-} in
    "") ;;
    *[!0-9]*|0)
      bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB must be a positive decimal KiB value, got '${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB}'"
      return 1 ;;
    *)
      [ "$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB" -le "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_DEFAULT_KIB" ] || {
        bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB may lower the phase worker floor (<= default ${BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_DEFAULT_KIB}) but not raise it, got '${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB}'"
        return 1
      }
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB=$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB ;;
  esac
  case ${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_PCT:-} in
    "") ;;
    *[!0-9]*|0)
      bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_PCT must be a positive decimal percent, got '${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_PCT}'"
      return 1 ;;
    *)
      [ "$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_PCT" -le "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_DEFAULT_PCT" ] || {
        bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_PCT may lower the phase worker margin (<= default ${BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_DEFAULT_PCT}) but not raise it, got '${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_PCT}'"
        return 1
      }
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_PCT=$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_PCT ;;
  esac
  case ${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB:-} in
    "") ;;
    *[!0-9]*|0)
      bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB must be a positive decimal KiB value, got '${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB}'"
      return 1 ;;
    *)
      [ "$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB" -le "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_DEFAULT_KIB" ] || {
        bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB may lower the phase base (<= default ${BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_DEFAULT_KIB}) but not raise it, got '${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB}'"
        return 1
      }
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB=$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB ;;
  esac
}

# bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_plan REQUESTED_WORKERS [REPO_ROOT]
# Prices the Stage 2 compiler-tests phase by its real per-worker need
# (BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB) instead of the compile-shard
# budget or a host fraction clamped to the compile-worker ceiling, both of
# which produced caps no worker count could pass (bug tree_rss_floor_kills_
# stage2_compiler_tests_on_large_hosts_2026-10-15, data points 5 and 6):
#     budget  = min(host_total x tree_rss_host_pct / 100, 3/4 x host_available)
#     workers = min(REQUESTED, (budget - base) / (floor x margin))   >= 1
#     cap     = base + workers x floor x margin
# The 3/4-of-available term is the bound the elevated-ceiling admission
# applies in both owners (bootstrap_tree_rss_admit_ceiling, the watchdog), so
# the plan never asks for what admission would refuse. Sets:
#     bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers      workers to run (REQUESTED is an upper bound)
#     bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib      the cap (kills a runaway above it)
#     bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_ceiling_kib  cap when it exceeds the default hard
#                                          ceiling for that worker count (needs
#                                          the elevated-ceiling admission), else 0
#     bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_budget_kib, bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound
#     (worker-floor | worker-floor-elevated), bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_summary
# Returns 1 with bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal naming the requirement when host
# RAM is unknown or the budget cannot hold ONE worker. Never clamps below the
# floor: fewer workers, or a refusal.
bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_plan() {
  btr_wb_requested=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_canonical_uint "${1:-}" 3)
  btr_wb_root=${2:-}
  bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal=
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers=0
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib=0
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_ceiling_kib=0
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_budget_kib=0
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound=refused
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_timeout_scale=1
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_summary=
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_cap_kib=0
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_ceiling_kib=0
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_bound=refused
  bootstrap_tree_rss_source=default
  [ -n "$btr_wb_requested" ] && [ "$btr_wb_requested" -ge 1 ] && [ "$btr_wb_requested" -le 128 ] || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: whole-build phase worker count must be a decimal 1..128, got '${1:-}'"
    return 1
  }
  bootstrap_tree_rss_probe_host || return 1
  bootstrap_tree_rss_phase_pricing_resolve || return 1
  btr_wb_worker=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_phase_worker_kib)
  btr_wb_one=$((BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB + btr_wb_worker))
  btr_wb_price="base ${BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB} KiB + worker floor ${BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB} KiB x ${BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_MARGIN_PCT}%"
  [ -n "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib" ] || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: whole-build phase needs host RAM evidence (host RAM unknown via ${bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source}): one full-CLI build worker requires ${btr_wb_one} KiB (${btr_wb_price}) and cannot be bounded without the host total"
    return 1
  }
  bootstrap_tree_rss_knob HOST_PCT tree_rss_host_pct "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT_DEFAULT" 2 "$btr_wb_root" || return 1
  btr_wb_pct=$btr_k_value
  [ "$btr_wb_pct" -le "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT_MAX" ] || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: tree_rss_host_pct=$btr_wb_pct exceeds $BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT_MAX"
    return 1
  }
  btr_wb_budget=$((bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib / 100 * btr_wb_pct))
  btr_wb_budget_bound="host RAM ${bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib} KiB x ${btr_wb_pct}%"
  if [ -n "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_available_kib" ]; then
    btr_wb_avail=$((bootstrap_tree_rss_host_available_kib / 4 * 3))
    if [ "$btr_wb_avail" -lt "$btr_wb_budget" ]; then
      btr_wb_budget=$btr_wb_avail
      btr_wb_budget_bound="3/4 of available ${bootstrap_tree_rss_host_available_kib} KiB"
    fi
  fi
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_budget_kib=$btr_wb_budget
  btr_wb_fit=$(((btr_wb_budget - BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB) / btr_wb_worker))
  btr_wb_small=0
  if [ "$btr_wb_fit" -lt 1 ]; then
    # Small-host single-worker mode (2026-11-06): the host cannot hold one
    # worker at floor x margin (24 GiB macOS arm64: ~18 GiB at 75% vs ~28 GiB).
    # Run exactly ONE worker under the host budget at the max host share
    # (still bounded by 3/4 of available); a runaway above that is killed.
    # Logged as small-host mode, never silent. Refused only when the budget
    # cannot even hold the phase base.
    btr_wb_sbudget=$((bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib / 100 * BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT_MAX))
    btr_wb_sbound="host RAM ${bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib} KiB x ${BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT_MAX}% (small-host max)"
    if [ -n "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_available_kib" ] && [ "$btr_wb_avail" -lt "$btr_wb_sbudget" ]; then
      btr_wb_sbudget=$btr_wb_avail
      btr_wb_sbound="3/4 of available ${bootstrap_tree_rss_host_available_kib} KiB"
    fi
    if [ "$btr_wb_sbudget" -gt "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB" ]; then
      btr_wb_small=1
      btr_wb_fit=1
      btr_wb_budget=$btr_wb_sbudget
      btr_wb_budget_bound=$btr_wb_sbound
      bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_budget_kib=$btr_wb_budget
    fi
  fi
  [ "$btr_wb_fit" -ge 1 ] || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: whole-build phase cannot fit one full-CLI build worker: host budget ${btr_wb_budget} KiB (${btr_wb_budget_bound}; host RAM via ${bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source}) is below the one-worker requirement ${btr_wb_one} KiB (${btr_wb_price}); free host memory (another lane?), raise tree_rss_host_pct (max ${BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT_MAX}), or lower the phase pricing for a warm-cache lane via SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB (<= ${BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB} KiB)"
    return 1
  }
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers=$btr_wb_fit
  [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers" -le "$btr_wb_requested" ] || bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers=$btr_wb_requested
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib=$((BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB + bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers * btr_wb_worker))
  [ "$btr_wb_small" = 0 ] || bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib=$btr_wb_budget
  btr_wb_default_ceiling=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib")
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound=worker-floor
  if [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib" -gt "$btr_wb_default_ceiling" ]; then
    bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_ceiling_kib=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib
    bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound=worker-floor-elevated
  fi
  if [ "$btr_wb_small" = 1 ]; then
    bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound=small-host-one-worker
    [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_ceiling_kib" = 0 ] || bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound=small-host-one-worker-elevated
    btr_wb_price="SMALL-HOST MODE: 1 worker under host budget (one-worker requirement $btr_wb_one KiB = $btr_wb_price exceeds it)"
  fi
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_timeout_scale=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_timeout_scale "$btr_wb_requested" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers")
  # compiler_cli_build row (BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB): the
  # plan cap by default; the row cap when >= 2 workers run, it is above the
  # plan cap and the host budget (same bound admission applies) holds it.
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_cap_kib=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_ceiling_kib=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_ceiling_kib
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_bound=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound
  btr_wb_cli=$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB
  btr_wb_cli_note=
  if [ "$btr_wb_small" = 0 ] && [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers" -ge 2 ] &&
     [ "$btr_wb_cli" -gt "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib" ]; then
    if [ "$btr_wb_cli" -le "$btr_wb_budget" ]; then
      bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_cap_kib=$btr_wb_cli
      bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_ceiling_kib=0
      [ "$btr_wb_cli" -le "$btr_wb_default_ceiling" ] || bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_ceiling_kib=$btr_wb_cli
      bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_bound=cli-row-mir-shards
      btr_wb_cli_note="; compiler_cli_build row cap ${btr_wb_cli} KiB (bound cli-row-mir-shards)"
    else
      btr_wb_cli_note="; compiler_cli_build row cap ${btr_wb_cli} KiB exceeds host budget ${btr_wb_budget} KiB, row keeps the plan cap"
    fi
  fi
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_summary="whole-build phase: workers ${bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers} (requested ${btr_wb_requested}, host budget fits ${btr_wb_fit}, timeout scale x${bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_timeout_scale}), cap ${bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib} KiB = ${btr_wb_price}$([ "$btr_wb_small" = 1 ] || printf ' x %s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers"), host budget ${btr_wb_budget} KiB (${btr_wb_budget_bound}; host RAM via ${bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source}), default ceiling ${btr_wb_default_ceiling} KiB, elevated ceiling ${bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_ceiling_kib} KiB, bound ${bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound}${btr_wb_cli_note}"
}

# bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_export REQUESTED_WORKERS [REPO_ROOT]
# Plans the phase and publishes the plan the way the campaign and per-row
# owners consume it:
#   SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB      the cap
#   SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB      only when the cap is above
#       the default ceiling: both owners then admit it through the existing
#       elevated-ceiling admission (3/4 of REAL total AND available host
#       memory, enforce mode, declared workers, no fixture hooks) and record
#       compiler_ceiling_admission=elevated in the receipt
#   BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS                 the fitted worker count, so
#       the compiler's own pool admission (cap x 60% / 9 GB) cannot start more
#       workers than the cap was priced for
#   SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE/_BOUND   receipt attribution
#   bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_timeout_scale  ceil(requested / fitted) bounded by
#       BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TIMEOUT_SCALE_MAX (1 for an explicit cap); callers
#       publish their time budgets through bootstrap_tree_rss_scaled_timeout
# An explicit SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB already in the
# environment is kept untouched (a monitored diagnostic attempt, not policy).
# Monitor mode enforces nothing, and the watchdog still refuses a cap above
# its default ceiling there (the elevated admission requires enforce mode),
# so in monitor mode the cap is clamped to the default ceiling and no ceiling
# is requested; the plan's numbers stay in bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_*.
# The published pair is then re-admitted through bootstrap_tree_rss_resolve
# WORKERS so a refusal (host headroom consumed by another lane, fixture hooks
# present, ...) is reported here with the owners' own reason, before the
# phase starts, instead of as an exit-125 receipt minutes later.
bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_export() {
  btr_we_requested=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_canonical_uint "${1:-}" 3)
  # Attribution is rebuilt by bootstrap_tree_rss_scaled_timeout per phase.
  BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SOURCE=
  bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_timeout_scale=1
  # The compiler_cli_build row cap is published only by an admitted
  # enforce-mode plan below; never inherited from a caller.
  unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CEILING_KIB \
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_BOUND
  if [ -n "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB:-}" ]; then
    # Kept as-is, but admitted NOW (over-ceiling is refused here, not by the
    # campaign minutes later) and the requested count is published unchanged
    # so the verifier does not fall back to its own default.
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal=
    [ -n "$btr_we_requested" ] && [ "$btr_we_requested" -ge 1 ] && [ "$btr_we_requested" -le 128 ] || {
      bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: whole-build phase worker count must be a decimal 1..128, got '${1:-}'"
      return 1
    }
    bootstrap_tree_rss_resolve "$btr_we_requested" "${2:-}" || return 1
    bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers=$btr_we_requested
    bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib=$bootstrap_tree_rss_cap_kib
    bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_ceiling_kib=0
    bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_budget_kib=0
    bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound=explicit
    BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS=$btr_we_requested
    export BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS
    bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_summary="whole-build phase: explicit SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB} KiB kept, not policy-priced (${bootstrap_tree_rss_summary}); workers ${bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers} as requested"
    return 0
  fi
  bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_plan "$@" || return 1
  SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib
  if [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_ceiling_kib" -gt 0 ]; then
    if [ "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE:-enforce}" = enforce ]; then
      SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_ceiling_kib
      export SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB
    else
      SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib")
      bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound=worker-floor-monitor-clamped
      bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_summary="${bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_summary}; monitor mode: cap clamped to the default ceiling ${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB} KiB, no elevated ceiling requested"
    fi
  fi
  BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers
  SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE=phase-policy
  SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound
  export SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS \
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND
  # compiler_cli_build row cap: published for the row owner
  # (bootstrap_tree_rss_row_cap_enter) and the campaign envelope only in
  # enforce mode (monitor mode cannot admit an elevated ceiling), and
  # re-admitted NOW through the same owner check as the phase pair, so a host
  # that cannot hold it refuses the phase here instead of mid-row.
  if [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_cap_kib" -gt "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib" ] &&
     [ "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE:-enforce}" = enforce ]; then
    btr_we_cli_refusal=$(
      SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_cap_kib
      SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_bound
      if [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_ceiling_kib" -gt 0 ]; then
        SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_ceiling_kib
        export SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB
      fi
      bootstrap_tree_rss_resolve "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers" "${2:-}" || {
        printf '%s' "${bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal:-refused}"
        exit 1
      }
    ) || {
      bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: compiler_cli_build row cap $bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_cap_kib KiB not admitted: $btr_we_cli_refusal"
      return 1
    }
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_cap_kib
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CEILING_KIB=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_ceiling_kib
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_BOUND=$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_bound
    export SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CEILING_KIB \
      SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_BOUND
  fi
  bootstrap_tree_rss_resolve "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers" "${2:-}" || return 1
}

# Validate the published compiler_cli_build row cap against the published
# phase pair. Sets btr_rc_cap/_ceiling/_bound; returns 1 with
# bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal on anything malformed or incoherent (fail closed).
bootstrap_tree_rss__cli_row_published() {
  btr_rc_cap=$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB
  btr_rc_ceiling=${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CEILING_KIB:-}
  btr_rc_bound=${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_BOUND:-}
  btr_rc_phase=${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB:-}
  case "$btr_rc_cap" in ''|0*|*[!0-9]*)
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB must be a canonical positive decimal KiB value, got '$btr_rc_cap'"; return 1 ;;
  esac
  case "$btr_rc_ceiling" in 0) ;; ''|0*|*[!0-9]*)
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CEILING_KIB must be 0 or a canonical positive decimal KiB value, got '$btr_rc_ceiling'"; return 1 ;;
  esac
  [ "${#btr_rc_cap}" -le 15 ] && [ "${#btr_rc_ceiling}" -le 15 ] || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal='tree RSS policy: compiler_cli_build row cap/ceiling is oversized'; return 1;
  }
  bootstrap_tree_rss_attribution_valid "$btr_rc_bound" || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: invalid SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_BOUND '$btr_rc_bound' (want [a-z][a-z-]{0,31})"; return 1;
  }
  case "$btr_rc_phase" in ''|0*|*[!0-9]*)
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: compiler_cli_build row cap $btr_rc_cap KiB published without a published phase cap"; return 1 ;;
  esac
  [ "${#btr_rc_phase}" -le 15 ] && [ "$btr_rc_cap" -gt "$btr_rc_phase" ] || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: compiler_cli_build row cap $btr_rc_cap KiB is at or below the phase cap $btr_rc_phase KiB"; return 1;
  }
  [ "$btr_rc_ceiling" = 0 ] || [ "$btr_rc_ceiling" -ge "$btr_rc_cap" ] || {
    bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal="tree RSS policy: compiler_cli_build row cap $btr_rc_cap KiB is above its ceiling $btr_rc_ceiling KiB"; return 1;
  }
}

# bootstrap_tree_rss_row_cap_enter TASK / bootstrap_tree_rss_row_cap_leave
# Scope the published compiler_cli_build row cap (whole_build_export) around
# that ONE row: the row owner then sees cap/ceiling/bound for the row, and
# leave restores the phase pair exactly (set-ness included) for the next row.
# Any other TASK, or no published row cap, is a no-op. Returns 1 with
# bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal when the published row cap is malformed: the
# caller must fail the row, never run it at the phase cap or a default.
bootstrap_tree_rss_row_cap_enter() {
  bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal=
  btr_rc_active=0
  [ "${1:-}" = compiler_cli_build ] || return 0
  [ -n "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB+x}" ] || return 0
  bootstrap_tree_rss__cli_row_published || return 1
  btr_rc_prev_cap=$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB
  btr_rc_prev_bound_set=${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND+x}
  btr_rc_prev_bound=${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND-}
  btr_rc_prev_ceiling_set=${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB+x}
  btr_rc_prev_ceiling=${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB-}
  SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=$btr_rc_cap
  SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND=$btr_rc_bound
  export SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND
  if [ "$btr_rc_ceiling" != 0 ]; then
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB=$btr_rc_ceiling
    export SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB
  fi
  btr_rc_active=1
}

bootstrap_tree_rss_row_cap_leave() {
  [ "${btr_rc_active:-0}" = 1 ] || return 0
  btr_rc_active=0
  SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=$btr_rc_prev_cap
  if [ -n "$btr_rc_prev_bound_set" ]; then
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND=$btr_rc_prev_bound
  else
    unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND
  fi
  if [ -n "$btr_rc_prev_ceiling_set" ]; then
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB=$btr_rc_prev_ceiling
  else
    unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB
  fi
}

# bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_envelope
# The campaign watchdog wraps every row of the phase, which run serially, so
# its cap is the LARGEST published row cap: the compiler_cli_build row cap
# when published (with its ceiling and bound), else the phase pair. Sets
# bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_{cap_kib,ceiling_kib,bound}; ceiling_kib is
# empty when no elevated ceiling is published. Returns 1 with
# bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal on a malformed published row cap.
bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_envelope() {
  bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal=
  bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_cap_kib=${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB:-5859375}
  bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_ceiling_kib=${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB:-}
  bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_bound=${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND:-unspecified}
  [ -n "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB+x}" ] || return 0
  bootstrap_tree_rss__cli_row_published || return 1
  bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_cap_kib=$btr_rc_cap
  [ "$btr_rc_ceiling" = 0 ] || bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_ceiling_kib=$btr_rc_ceiling
  bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_bound=$btr_rc_bound
}

# Worker count of a compiler command line: the value of the last --threads /
# --jobs (separate or `=` form). Prints 0 when the command declares none.
bootstrap_tree_rss_command_jobs() {
  btr_cj=0
  btr_cj_next=0
  for btr_cj_arg in "$@"; do
    if [ "$btr_cj_next" = 1 ]; then
      btr_cj_next=0
      btr_cj_value=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_canonical_uint "$btr_cj_arg" 3)
      [ -z "$btr_cj_value" ] || btr_cj=$btr_cj_value
      continue
    fi
    case "$btr_cj_arg" in
      --threads|--jobs) btr_cj_next=1 ;;
      --threads=*|--jobs=*)
        btr_cj_value=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_canonical_uint "${btr_cj_arg#*=}" 3)
        [ -z "$btr_cj_value" ] || btr_cj=$btr_cj_value ;;
    esac
  done
  printf '%s\n' "$btr_cj"
}

bootstrap_tree_rss__selftest() {
  btr_st_dir=$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/tree-rss-policy.XXXXXX") || return 2
  btr_st_fail=0
  btr_st_n=0
  printf 'MemTotal:       134094232 kB\n' >"$btr_st_dir/big"
  printf 'MemTotal:        16000000 kB\n' >"$btr_st_dir/small"
  printf 'MemTotal:         5000000 kB\n' >"$btr_st_dir/tiny"
  : >"$btr_st_dir/none"
  # The 2026-11-05 incident host (121 GiB aarch64), idle and with another
  # lane holding most of it (MemAvailable 40 GB), and a 64 GiB host.
  printf 'MemTotal:       127600812 kB\nMemFree:        90000000 kB\nMemAvailable:   112044352 kB\n' >"$btr_st_dir/aarch64"
  printf 'MemTotal:       127600812 kB\nMemFree:        30000000 kB\nMemAvailable:    40000000 kB\n' >"$btr_st_dir/aarch64-busy"
  printf 'MemTotal:        66865260 kB\nMemAvailable:    60000000 kB\n' >"$btr_st_dir/host64"
  # Same host, a lane holding ~40 GiB: 3/4 of 80000000 = 60000000 KiB still
  # fits 2 workers (54525952) but not the 62914560 KiB compiler_cli_build row.
  printf 'MemTotal:       127600812 kB\nMemFree:        70000000 kB\nMemAvailable:    80000000 kB\n' >"$btr_st_dir/aarch64-tight"
  printf 'host_config:\n  schema: simple-host-config-v1\n  tree_rss_per_job_mib: 200\n' >"$btr_st_dir/good.sdn"
  printf 'host_config:\n  schema: simple-host-config-v1\n  tree_rss_per_job_mib: many\n' >"$btr_st_dir/bad.sdn"
  printf 'host_config:\n  schema: simple-host-config-v1\n  tree_rss_host_pct: 90\n' >"$btr_st_dir/pct.sdn"
  btr_st_root=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")/../../.." && pwd -P) || btr_st_root=
  # expect LABEL MEMINFO JOBS EXPLICIT_CAP WANT [SETUP]
  #   WANT = cap:ceiling:bound:source, or REFUSED (a refusal WITH a reason)
  #   MEMINFO `real` uses the live host and no fixture
  btr_st_expect() {
    btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
    btr_st_got=$(
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_BASE_MIB SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT
      unset SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_BASE_MIB SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_WORKER_MEM_MIB SIMPLE_HOST_WORKER_MEM_MIB
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND
      [ -z "$4" ] || SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=$4
      unset BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG SIMPLE_HOST_ENV_FILE
      SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE=monitor
      # Fixtures price the fanout (HIR) default on every host; the Windows
      # pricing is pinned by its own fixture below.
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB_DEFAULT=5120
      btr_st_use_root=
      if [ "$2" != real ]; then
        BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH="$btr_st_dir/$2"
        BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE=1
      fi
      [ -z "${6:-}" ] || eval "$6"
      [ -z "${SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG:-}" ] || export SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG
      if bootstrap_tree_rss_resolve "$3" "$btr_st_use_root"; then
        printf '%s:%s:%s:%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_cap_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_bound" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_source"
      else
        [ -n "$bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal" ] && printf REFUSED || printf SILENT-REFUSAL
      fi
    )
    if [ "$btr_st_got" != "$5" ]; then
      echo "selftest FAIL: $1: want $5 got $btr_st_got" >&2
      btr_st_fail=1
    fi
  }
  # Historical behaviour is unchanged while no worker count is declared.
  btr_st_expect undeclared-keeps-floor big 0 '' 5859375:50331648:floor:default
  # HIR pricing (fanout host, 5120 MiB/job): 8 jobs = 3 GiB + 40 GiB, which the
  # compiler's clamp turns into exactly 8 admitted HIR workers (x60% / 3000000).
  btr_st_expect eight-jobs-price-hir-workers big 8 '' 45088768:50331648:budget:default
  # Windows pricing (frontend pinned, 96 MiB codegen shard): 8 jobs keep the floor.
  # Windows pricing falls to the floor, which the host-scaled default lifts to
  # (base + jobs * 3300 MiB) -- 3072 + 8 * 3300 MiB -- under 60% of host RAM.
  btr_st_expect eight-jobs-windows-price-host-scaled big 8 '' 30179328:50331648:host-scaled:default BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB_DEFAULT=96
  # The incident host (128 GB, 80 jobs, worker_mem_mib 1200): 60% of RAM, not 5.59 GiB.
  btr_st_expect windows-128gb-80-jobs-host-scaled big 80 '' 80456520:87031808:host-scaled:default 'BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB_DEFAULT=96 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_WORKER_MEM_MIB=1200'
  btr_st_expect windows-16gb-80-jobs-small small 80 '' 8000000:50331648:host-fraction:default 'BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB_DEFAULT=96 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_WORKER_MEM_MIB=1200'
  btr_st_expect windows-unknown-host-keeps-budget none 80 '' 11010048:50331648:budget:default 'BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB_DEFAULT=96 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_WORKER_MEM_MIB=1200'
  btr_st_expect windows-explicit-cap-bypasses-scale big 80 20000000 20000000:87031808:explicit:explicit-env 'BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB_DEFAULT=96'
  btr_st_expect windows-garbage-worker-mem-uses-default big 8 '' 30179328:50331648:host-scaled:default 'BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB_DEFAULT=96 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_WORKER_MEM_MIB=lots'
  # Beyond that the host fraction and the hard ceiling bound the tree.
  btr_st_expect nineteen-jobs-hit-ceiling big 19 '' 50331648:50331648:hard-ceiling:default
  # The incident: 80 jobs needs more than the old 6 GB / 7 GB pair.
  btr_st_expect eighty-jobs-scale big 80 '' 67047100:87031808:host-fraction:default
  btr_st_expect forty-jobs-scale big 40 '' 50331648:50331648:hard-ceiling:default
  # Monotone in the worker count.
  btr_st_expect hard-max-jobs big 128 '' 67047100:100570674:host-fraction:default
  # Host fraction: a 16 GB host never hands half its RAM plus to one tree.
  btr_st_expect small-host-fraction small 80 '' 8000000:50331648:host-fraction:default
  # Unknown host RAM is no evidence: the job-scaled budget applies, but nothing
  # widens the ceiling beyond the static value.
  btr_st_expect unknown-host-fails-closed none 80 '' 50331648:50331648:hard-ceiling:default
  # Explicit cap: honoured under the ceiling, refused (not clamped) above it.
  btr_st_expect explicit-under-ceiling big 80 20000000 20000000:87031808:explicit:explicit-env
  btr_st_expect explicit-over-ceiling-refused big 80 87031809 REFUSED
  btr_st_expect explicit-over-static-refused big 0 51000000 REFUSED
  btr_st_expect explicit-garbage-refused big 80 lots REFUSED
  # Knob overrides, and their fail-closed validation.
  btr_st_expect knob-per-job big 80 '' 19529728:87031808:budget:env-knobs SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB=200
  btr_st_expect knob-host-env big 80 '' 67047100:87031808:host-fraction:env-knobs SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_BASE_MIB=5120
  btr_st_expect knob-host-env-base-few-jobs big 8 '' 47185920:50331648:budget:env-knobs SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_BASE_MIB=5120
  btr_st_expect knob-runaway-hits-ceiling big 80 '' 87031808:87031808:hard-ceiling:env-knobs 'SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB=4096 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT=75'
  btr_st_expect knob-pct-over-max-refused big 80 '' REFUSED SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT=90
  btr_st_expect knob-garbage-refused big 80 '' REFUSED SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB=many
  btr_st_expect jobs-out-of-range-refused big 129 '' REFUSED
  # Leading zeros: 08/09 used to crash $(( )) and 040 was read as octal 32.
  btr_st_expect jobs-leading-zero-08 big 08 '' 45088768:50331648:budget:default
  btr_st_expect jobs-leading-zero-040 big 040 '' 50331648:50331648:hard-ceiling:default
  btr_st_expect jobs-leading-zero-0080 big 0080 '' 67047100:87031808:host-fraction:default
  btr_st_expect jobs-junk-refused big 8x '' REFUSED
  btr_st_expect jobs-negative-refused big -8 '' REFUSED
  # The host memory fixture can raise the ceiling, so it is a gated test hook:
  # refused without its switch, refused while the cap is enforced.
  btr_st_expect fixture-without-switch-refused big 80 '' REFUSED 'unset BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE'
  btr_st_expect fixture-in-enforce-refused big 80 '' REFUSED 'SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE=enforce'
  btr_st_expect fixture-in-default-mode-refused big 80 '' REFUSED 'unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE'
  # Host config file layer: a valid value is attributed, an invalid one is a
  # refusal (host-env.shs alone would warn and fall through to the default).
  if [ -n "$btr_st_root" ] && [ -f "$btr_st_root/scripts/setup/host-env.shs" ]; then
    btr_st_expect config-file-knob big 80 '' 19529728:87031808:budget:host-config \
      'SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG=$btr_st_dir/good.sdn; btr_st_use_root=$btr_st_root'
    btr_st_expect config-file-garbage-refused big 80 '' REFUSED \
      'SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG=$btr_st_dir/bad.sdn; btr_st_use_root=$btr_st_root'
    btr_st_expect config-file-pct-over-max-refused big 80 '' REFUSED \
      'SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG=$btr_st_dir/pct.sdn; btr_st_use_root=$btr_st_root'
  else
    echo 'selftest FAIL: host-env.shs not found; config-file fixtures did not run' >&2
    btr_st_fail=1
  fi
  # Whole-build phase cap: host fraction clamped to the jobs-scaled ceiling on
  # a large host; a small host keeps its host-fraction bound.
  for btr_st_pc in big:50331648 small:8000000; do
    btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
    btr_st_got=$(
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG SIMPLE_HOST_ENV_FILE
      SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE=monitor
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH="$btr_st_dir/${btr_st_pc%%:*}"
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE=1
      bootstrap_tree_rss_resolve 12 '' && bootstrap_tree_rss_phase_cap_kib ''
    )
    [ "$btr_st_got" = "${btr_st_pc#*:}" ] || {
      echo "selftest FAIL: phase-cap-${btr_st_pc%%:*}: want ${btr_st_pc#*:} got $btr_st_got" >&2
      btr_st_fail=1
    }
  done
  # Stage2 native-build at 16 workers uses the same phase pricing: a 128 GB
  # host gets well above the floor (not the floor as ceiling); a 16 GB host
  # stays within its host fraction.
  for btr_st_pc in big:above small:bounded; do
    btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
    btr_st_got=$(
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG SIMPLE_HOST_ENV_FILE
      SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE=monitor
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH="$btr_st_dir/${btr_st_pc%%:*}"
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE=1
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PER_JOB_MIB_DEFAULT=96 bootstrap_tree_rss_resolve 16 '' && bootstrap_tree_rss_phase_cap_kib ''
    )
    case "${btr_st_pc#*:}" in
      above) [ "${btr_st_got:-0}" -gt "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_FLOOR_KIB" ] && [ "$btr_st_got" -le 50331648 ] ;;
      *) [ "${btr_st_got:-0}" -ge "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_FLOOR_KIB" ] && [ "$btr_st_got" -le 8000000 ] ;;
    esac || {
      echo "selftest FAIL: native-build-phase-cap-${btr_st_pc%%:*}: got $btr_st_got" >&2
      btr_st_fail=1
    }
  done
  # Worker count is read from the command the cap will actually govern.
  btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
  [ "$(bootstrap_tree_rss_command_jobs simple native-build --threads 80 -o x)" = 80 ] &&
    [ "$(bootstrap_tree_rss_command_jobs simple native-build --threads=40)" = 40 ] &&
    [ "$(bootstrap_tree_rss_command_jobs simple native-build -o x)" = 0 ] &&
    [ "$(bootstrap_tree_rss_command_jobs simple --threads many)" = 0 ] &&
    [ "$(bootstrap_tree_rss_command_jobs simple --threads 08)" = 8 ] &&
    [ "$(bootstrap_tree_rss_command_jobs simple --threads=040)" = 40 ] || {
    echo 'selftest FAIL: command worker count' >&2
    btr_st_fail=1
  }
  # workers = cap / per-worker: 128 GB host fits >= 40 (full CPU use), 16 GB stays small.
  btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
  [ "$(bootstrap_tree_rss_workers_fit 80456520 1200)" -ge 40 ] &&
    [ "$(bootstrap_tree_rss_workers_fit 9600000 1200)" -le 8 ] || {
    echo 'selftest FAIL: workers fit by cap' >&2
    btr_st_fail=1
  }
  # Whole-build phase plan: priced per worker at the floor, workers reduced to
  # fit, never capped below the floor, refused when one worker cannot fit.
  # plan LABEL MEMINFO REQUESTED WANT [SETUP]
  #   WANT = workers:cap:ceiling:bound, or REFUSED=<substring of the reason>
  btr_st_plan() {
    btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
    btr_st_got=$(
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG SIMPLE_HOST_ENV_FILE
      SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE=monitor
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH="$btr_st_dir/$2"
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE=1
      [ -z "${5:-}" ] || eval "$5"
      if bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_plan "$3" ''; then
        printf '%s:%s:%s:%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib" \
          "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_ceiling_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound"
      else
        printf 'REFUSED=%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal"
      fi
    )
    case "$4" in
      REFUSED=*) case "$btr_st_got" in REFUSED=*"${4#REFUSED=}"*) return 0 ;; esac ;;
      *) [ "$btr_st_got" = "$4" ] && return 0 ;;
    esac
    echo "selftest FAIL: plan-$1: want $4 got $btr_st_got" >&2
    btr_st_fail=1
  }
  # 121 GiB host, 8 build threads: 50% of RAM = 63800400 KiB holds 2 workers
  # at 25165824 KiB each (16 GiB x 150%) over the 4 GiB base, so the plan runs
  # 2 (not 8), caps at 54525952 KiB (>= 16 GiB per worker: 26 GiB each) and
  # requests that as the elevated ceiling (default ceiling 48 GiB).
  btr_st_plan aarch64-8-threads aarch64 8 2:54525952:54525952:worker-floor-elevated
  # Runaway: the cap is base + workers x floor x margin, finite and strictly
  # below the host budget (63800400 KiB), never the host total or fraction.
  btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
  btr_st_got=$(
    unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB
    unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG SIMPLE_HOST_ENV_FILE
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE=monitor
    BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH="$btr_st_dir/aarch64"
    BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE=1
    bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_plan 8 '' || exit 1
    [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib" -lt "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_budget_kib" ] &&
      [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib" -eq $((BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_BASE_KIB + 2 * 25165824)) ] &&
      printf 'cap-below-budget:%s<%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_budget_kib"
  )
  [ "$btr_st_got" = 'cap-below-budget:54525952<63800400' ] || {
    echo "selftest FAIL: plan-aarch64-runaway-cap-is-finite: got $btr_st_got" >&2
    btr_st_fail=1
  }
  # One requested worker keeps one worker, cap 29360128 KiB, under the default
  # ceiling: no elevated ceiling needed (the 5859375 floor is gone).
  btr_st_plan aarch64-1-thread aarch64 1 1:29360128:0:worker-floor
  # Another lane holds the host: 3/4 of 40 GB available = 30000000 KiB fits
  # exactly one worker -- workers reduced, cap still >= the floor.
  btr_st_plan aarch64-busy-reduces-workers aarch64-busy 8 1:29360128:0:worker-floor
  # 64 GiB host (the 2026-10-15 incident host): 50% = 33432630 fits 1 worker.
  btr_st_plan host64-one-worker host64 8 1:29360128:0:worker-floor
  # 128 GB Windows host: 67047100 budget -> 2 workers, elevated.
  btr_st_plan big-two-workers big 12 2:54525952:54525952:worker-floor-elevated
  # tree_rss_host_pct 75 on the 121 GiB host: 95700600 -> 3 workers, elevated.
  btr_st_plan aarch64-pct75-three-workers aarch64 8 3:79691776:79691776:worker-floor-elevated SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT=75
  # Tiny host: 16 GB x 50% = 8000000 KiB < one worker (29360128): fail closed,
  # naming the requirement.
  # Small host (16 GB): below one worker at floor x margin -> small-host
  # single-worker mode at 75% of RAM (12000000 KiB), cap = that budget.
  btr_st_plan small-host-one-worker small 8 1:12000000:0:small-host-one-worker
  btr_st_plan small-host-ignores-default-pct small 1 1:12000000:0:small-host-one-worker SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT=50
  # Even the max share cannot hold the 4 GiB phase base: still refused.
  btr_st_plan tiny-host-fails-closed tiny 8 'REFUSED=cannot fit one full-CLI build worker'
  btr_st_plan tiny-host-names-floor tiny 8 'REFUSED=worker floor 16777216 KiB x 150%'
  # Unknown host RAM is no evidence: refused, not floored.
  btr_st_plan unknown-host-fails-closed none 8 'REFUSED=needs host RAM evidence'
  btr_st_plan junk-workers-refused aarch64 8x 'REFUSED=worker count must be a decimal 1..128'
  btr_st_plan zero-workers-refused aarch64 0 'REFUSED=worker count must be a decimal 1..128'
  btr_st_plan pct-over-max-refused aarch64 8 'REFUSED=exceeds 75' SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT=90
  # compiler_cli_build row cap (run 11, 2026-11-06): a 2-worker plan prices
  # that ONE row at BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB when the host
  # budget holds it; every other row keeps the plan cap, and the plan cap
  # itself is unchanged. cli-plan LABEL MEMINFO REQUESTED WANT [SETUP]
  #   WANT = row_cap:row_ceiling:row_bound:plan_cap:plan_ceiling
  btr_st_cli_plan() {
    btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
    btr_st_got=$(
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG SIMPLE_HOST_ENV_FILE
      SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE=monitor
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH="$btr_st_dir/$2"
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE=1
      [ -z "${5:-}" ] || eval "$5"
      bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_plan "$3" '' || { printf 'REFUSED=%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal"; exit 0; }
      printf '%s:%s:%s:%s:%s' "${bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_cap_kib:-unset}" \
        "${bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_ceiling_kib:-unset}" "${bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_bound:-unset}" \
        "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_ceiling_kib"
    )
    [ "$btr_st_got" = "$4" ] || {
      echo "selftest FAIL: cli-plan-$1: want $4 got $btr_st_got" >&2
      btr_st_fail=1
    }
  }
  # Run-11 host: 60 GiB row, admitted as an elevated ceiling; phase stays 52 GiB.
  btr_st_cli_plan aarch64-cli-row-60g aarch64 8 62914560:62914560:cli-row-mir-shards:54525952:54525952
  btr_st_cli_plan big-cli-row-60g big 12 62914560:62914560:cli-row-mir-shards:54525952:54525952
  # Budget 60000000 < 62914560: the host cannot afford it -> row keeps the plan cap.
  btr_st_cli_plan aarch64-tight-keeps-plan aarch64-tight 8 54525952:54525952:worker-floor-elevated:54525952:54525952
  # One worker (no MIR shard pair) or a plan already above 60 GiB: unchanged.
  btr_st_cli_plan one-worker-keeps-plan aarch64 1 29360128:0:worker-floor:29360128:0
  btr_st_cli_plan host64-keeps-plan host64 8 29360128:0:worker-floor:29360128:0
  btr_st_cli_plan pct75-keeps-plan aarch64 8 79691776:79691776:worker-floor-elevated:79691776:79691776 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT=75
  btr_st_cli_plan small-host-keeps-plan small 8 12000000:0:small-host-one-worker:12000000:0
  # Row / campaign consumers of a PUBLISHED plan (enforce-mode values, no host
  # probe): row-cap TASK SETUP -> cap:ceiling:bound inside, then restored.
  btr_st_pub='SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=54525952 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB=54525952
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE=phase-policy SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND=worker-floor-elevated
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB=62914560 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CEILING_KIB=62914560
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_BOUND=cli-row-mir-shards'
  btr_st_row() {
    btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
    btr_st_got=$(
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CEILING_KIB SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_BOUND
      eval "export $3"
      bootstrap_tree_rss_row_cap_enter "$2" || { printf 'REFUSED=%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal"; exit 0; }
      btr_st_in="$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB:${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB:-unset}:$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND"
      bootstrap_tree_rss_row_cap_leave
      printf '%s|%s:%s:%s' "$btr_st_in" "$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB" \
        "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB:-unset}" "$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND"
    )
    case "$4" in
      REFUSED=*) case "$btr_st_got" in REFUSED=*"${4#REFUSED=}"*) return 0 ;; esac ;;
      *) [ "$btr_st_got" = "$4" ] && return 0 ;;
    esac
    echo "selftest FAIL: row-cap-$1: want $4 got $btr_st_got" >&2
    btr_st_fail=1
  }
  btr_st_back='54525952:54525952:worker-floor-elevated'
  btr_st_row cli-gets-60g compiler_cli_build "$btr_st_pub" "62914560:62914560:cli-row-mir-shards|$btr_st_back"
  btr_st_row runner-keeps-plan test_runner_build "$btr_st_pub" "$btr_st_back|$btr_st_back"
  btr_st_row mcp-keeps-plan mcp_build "$btr_st_pub" "$btr_st_back|$btr_st_back"
  btr_st_row cli-without-row-cap compiler_cli_build 'SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=54525952 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB=54525952 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE=phase-policy SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND=worker-floor-elevated' \
    "$btr_st_back|$btr_st_back"
  btr_st_row malformed-row-cap-refused compiler_cli_build "$btr_st_pub SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB=6x" 'REFUSED=CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB'
  btr_st_row row-cap-below-phase-refused compiler_cli_build "$btr_st_pub SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB=1000" 'REFUSED=below the phase cap'
  btr_st_row row-cap-over-ceiling-refused compiler_cli_build "$btr_st_pub SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CEILING_KIB=60000000" 'REFUSED=above its ceiling'
  btr_st_row row-cap-without-phase-refused compiler_cli_build 'SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB=62914560 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CEILING_KIB=62914560 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_BOUND=cli-row-mir-shards' \
    'REFUSED=without a published phase cap'
  # The campaign watchdog encloses every (serial) row, so its envelope is the
  # largest row cap; without a published row cap it is the phase pair.
  btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
  btr_st_got=$(
    eval "export $btr_st_pub"
    bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_envelope || { printf 'REFUSED=%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal"; exit 0; }
    printf '%s:%s:%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_cap_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_ceiling_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_bound"
    unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CEILING_KIB SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_BOUND
    bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_envelope || exit 0
    printf '|%s:%s:%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_cap_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_ceiling_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_campaign_bound"
  )
  [ "$btr_st_got" = "62914560:62914560:cli-row-mir-shards|54525952:54525952:worker-floor-elevated" ] || {
    echo "selftest FAIL: campaign envelope: got $btr_st_got" >&2
    btr_st_fail=1
  }
  # Export under a fixture (monitor mode only, by the probe's own gate): the
  # elevated plan is clamped to the default ceiling, no ceiling env is set,
  # the thread count is the fitted one, and the pair re-admits.
  btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
  btr_st_got=$(
    unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB
    unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG SIMPLE_HOST_ENV_FILE BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE=monitor
    BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH="$btr_st_dir/aarch64"
    BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE=1
    bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_export 8 '' || { printf 'REFUSED=%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal"; exit 0; }
    printf '%s:%s:%s:%s:%s:%s' "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB:-}" "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB:-unset}" \
      "${BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS:-}" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_cap_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_source"
    printf ':%s' "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_CLI_ROW_CAP_KIB:-unset}"
  )
  [ "$btr_st_got" = '50331648:unset:2:worker-floor-monitor-clamped:50331648:phase-policy:unset' ] || {
    echo "selftest FAIL: whole-build export under monitor fixture: got $btr_st_got" >&2
    btr_st_fail=1
  }
  # Time budgets scale with the worker reduction: ceil(requested / fitted),
  # bounded by BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TIMEOUT_SCALE_MAX (run 4, 2026-11-05: 8 -> 2
  # workers, MIR workers killed at the unscaled 1800 s internal timeout).
  for btr_st_ts in 8:2:4 8:1:4 8:8:1 1:1:1 3:2:2 8:3:3 128:1:4 2:4:1 x:2:1 8:0:1; do
    btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
    btr_st_got=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_timeout_scale "${btr_st_ts%%:*}" "$(echo "$btr_st_ts" | cut -d: -f2)")
    [ "$btr_st_got" = "${btr_st_ts##*:}" ] || {
      echo "selftest FAIL: timeout-scale-$btr_st_ts: got $btr_st_got" >&2
      btr_st_fail=1
    }
  done
  # timeout-plan LABEL MEMINFO REQUESTED WANT [SETUP]: WANT = workers:scale:
  # native:row:campaign:source after the export and the three published budgets
  # (defaults 1800 / 3600 / 7200, the from-scratch Linux defaults).
  btr_st_timeout_plan() {
    btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
    btr_st_got=$(
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG SIMPLE_HOST_ENV_FILE BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS
      unset BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_NATIVE_INTERNAL_TIMEOUT BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_CAMPAIGN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
      unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND
      BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SOURCE=stale-from-caller
      SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE=monitor
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH="$btr_st_dir/$2"
      BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE=1
      [ -z "${5:-}" ] || eval "$5"
      bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_export "$3" '' || { printf 'REFUSED=%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal"; exit 0; }
      bootstrap_tree_rss_scaled_timeout BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_NATIVE_INTERNAL_TIMEOUT 1800 &&
        bootstrap_tree_rss_scaled_timeout BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS 3600 &&
        bootstrap_tree_rss_scaled_timeout BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_CAMPAIGN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS 7200 ||
        { printf 'REFUSED=%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal"; exit 0; }
      printf '%s:%s:%s:%s:%s:%s' "$BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS" "$BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SCALE" \
        "$BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_NATIVE_INTERNAL_TIMEOUT" "$BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS" \
        "$BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_CAMPAIGN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS" "$BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SOURCE"
    )
    [ "$btr_st_got" = "$4" ] && return 0
    echo "selftest FAIL: timeout-plan-$1: want $4 got $btr_st_got" >&2
    btr_st_fail=1
  }
  btr_st_pp=BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_NATIVE_INTERNAL_TIMEOUT:phase-policy-scaled,BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:phase-policy-scaled,BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_CAMPAIGN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:phase-policy-scaled
  # Run 4's shape: 8 requested, 2 fitted -> x4 on every default budget.
  btr_st_timeout_plan aarch64-8-to-2-scales-x4 aarch64 8 "2:4:7200:14400:28800:$btr_st_pp"
  # 8 requested, 1 fitted -> ceil 8, bounded to x4 (never unbounded).
  btr_st_timeout_plan busy-8-to-1-bounded-x4 aarch64-busy 8 "1:4:7200:14400:28800:$btr_st_pp"
  # No reduction -> budgets unchanged.
  btr_st_timeout_plan no-reduction-unchanged aarch64 1 \
    "1:1:1800:3600:7200:BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_NATIVE_INTERNAL_TIMEOUT:phase-policy,BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:phase-policy,BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_CAMPAIGN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:phase-policy"
  # Explicit user timeouts are honoured verbatim even when workers shrink.
  btr_st_timeout_plan explicit-timeouts-unchanged aarch64 8 \
    "2:4:900:1000:5000:BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_NATIVE_INTERNAL_TIMEOUT:explicit,BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:explicit,BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_CAMPAIGN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:explicit" \
    'BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_NATIVE_INTERNAL_TIMEOUT=900 BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1000 BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_CAMPAIGN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=5000'
  # An explicit cap is not policy-priced: workers as requested, no scaling.
  btr_st_timeout_plan explicit-cap-unscaled aarch64 8 \
    "8:1:1800:3600:7200:BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_NATIVE_INTERNAL_TIMEOUT:phase-policy,BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:phase-policy,BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_CAMPAIGN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:phase-policy" \
    'unset BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE; SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=12582912'
  # A malformed default is refused, never substituted.
  btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
  btr_st_got=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_scaled_timeout BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS 36x0 && printf ADMITTED || printf 'REFUSED=%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal")
  case "$btr_st_got" in
    'REFUSED=tree RSS policy: default timeout for BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS must be a positive decimal'*) ;;
    *) echo "selftest FAIL: scaled-timeout malformed default: $btr_st_got" >&2; btr_st_fail=1 ;;
  esac
  # An explicit cap is kept as-is (a monitored diagnostic attempt, not policy):
  # nothing is re-priced, but it is admitted up front, the requested thread
  # count is published unchanged, and it keeps the explicit-env attribution.
  btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
  btr_st_got=$(
    unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS
    unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=12582912
    bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_export 8 '' || { printf 'REFUSED=%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal"; exit 0; }
    printf '%s:%s:%s:%s:%s:%s' "$SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB" "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB:-unset}" \
      "${BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS:-unset}" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_source" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_bound"
  )
  [ "$btr_st_got" = '12582912:unset:8:explicit:explicit-env:explicit' ] || {
    echo "selftest FAIL: whole-build export keeps an explicit cap: got $btr_st_got" >&2
    btr_st_fail=1
  }
  # An explicit cap above the hard ceiling is refused by the export itself.
  btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
  btr_st_got=$(
    unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS
    unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=51000000
    bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_export 8 '' && printf ADMITTED || printf 'REFUSED=%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal"
  )
  case "$btr_st_got" in
    'REFUSED=tree RSS policy: SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB=51000000 KiB exceeds the hard ceiling'*) ;;
    *) echo "selftest FAIL: whole-build export admitted an over-ceiling explicit cap: $btr_st_got" >&2; btr_st_fail=1 ;;
  esac
  # Attribution: a diagnostic pair (no attribution vars) is explicit-env in
  # every owner; the published phase-policy attribution replaces it; a
  # malformed spelling is refused, not laundered.
  btr_st_expect diagnostic-pair-is-explicit-env big 8 12582912 12582912:50331648:explicit:explicit-env \
    'unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND'
  btr_st_expect published-attribution-wins big 8 12582912 12582912:50331648:worker-floor-elevated:phase-policy \
    'SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE=phase-policy SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND=worker-floor-elevated'
  btr_st_expect published-attribution-malformed-refused big 8 12582912 REFUSED \
    'SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE="Phase Policy" SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND=worker-floor'
  btr_st_expect published-attribution-half-refused big 8 12582912 REFUSED \
    'SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE=phase-policy; unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND'
  # Attribution vars without an explicit cap change nothing (policy-priced).
  btr_st_expect attribution-without-cap-ignored big 8 '' 45088768:50331648:budget:default \
    'SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_SOURCE=phase-policy SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_BOUND=worker-floor'
  # The real host, enforce mode, no fixture: the published pair is admitted
  # by the policy's own elevated-ceiling admission (real /proc/meminfo) when
  # 3/4 of the host's current MemAvailable still covers the cap, and refused
  # with the owners' reason otherwise; a host too small for one worker is
  # refused naming the requirement. Every branch is asserted, none skipped.
  btr_st_n=$((btr_st_n + 1))
  btr_st_got=$(
    unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_HOST_TREE_RSS_HOST_PCT SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_CAP_KIB
    unset SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB SIMPLE_HOST_CONFIG SIMPLE_HOST_ENV_FILE BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS
    unset BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE
    unset SIMPLE_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_MEMINFO_PATH SIMPLE_PROCESS_TREE_RSS_TEST_FIXTURE
    SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_RSS_CAP_MODE=enforce
    btr_st_avail=$(bootstrap_tree_rss_meminfo_available /proc/meminfo)
    if bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_export 8 ''; then
      btr_st_per=$((bootstrap_tree_rss_cap_kib / BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS))
      if [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_ceiling_kib" -gt 0 ]; then
        [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_admission" = elevated ] &&
          [ "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB:-}" = "$bootstrap_tree_rss_cap_kib" ] || { printf 'elevated-not-admitted:%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_summary"; exit 0; }
      else
        [ -z "${SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_COMPILER_RSS_CEILING_KIB+x}" ] || { printf 'ceiling-set-without-need'; exit 0; }
      fi
      [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_cap_kib" -eq "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib" ] &&
        [ "$BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS" -ge 1 ] && [ "$BOOTSTRAP_VERIFY_BUILD_THREADS" -le 8 ] &&
        [ "$btr_st_per" -ge "$BOOTSTRAP_TREE_RSS_PHASE_WORKER_FLOOR_KIB" ] &&
        [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_source" = phase-policy ] &&
        [ "$bootstrap_tree_rss_bound" = "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound" ] && printf ADMITTED || printf 'wrong-export:%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_summary"
    else
      case "$bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal" in
        (*'cannot fit one full-CLI build worker'*'worker floor 16777216 KiB'*) printf TOO-SMALL ;;
        (*'compiler ceiling '*' refused (previous='*'available_bound='*)
          # Only a real headroom shortfall may refuse here: the plan was
          # within 3/4 of MemAvailable at plan time, admission re-read it.
          [ -n "$btr_st_avail" ] && printf HEADROOM-REFUSED || printf 'refused-without-headroom-evidence' ;;
        (*) printf 'REFUSED=%s' "$bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal" ;;
      esac
    fi
  )
  case "$btr_st_got" in
    ADMITTED|TOO-SMALL|HEADROOM-REFUSED) ;;
    *) echo "selftest FAIL: whole-build export on the real host: $btr_st_got" >&2; btr_st_fail=1 ;;
  esac
  rm -rf "$btr_st_dir"
  if [ "$btr_st_fail" -ne 0 ]; then
    echo "FAIL — tree RSS policy selftest ($btr_st_n fixture(s))"
    return 1
  fi
  echo "PASS — $btr_st_n fixture(s) checked, tree RSS policy scales with workers and fails closed"
}

case "${0##*/}" in
  tree-rss-policy.shs)
    case "${1:-}" in
      --selftest) bootstrap_tree_rss__selftest; exit $? ;;
      --resolve)
        [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { echo "usage: $0 --resolve JOBS [REPO_ROOT]" >&2; exit 2; }
        if bootstrap_tree_rss_resolve "$2" "${3:-}"; then
          printf 'cap_kib=%s\nceiling_kib=%s\nhost_total_kib=%s\nhost_total_source=%s\nsource=%s\nbound=%s\n' \
            "$bootstrap_tree_rss_cap_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_ceiling_kib" \
            "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source" \
            "$bootstrap_tree_rss_source" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_bound"
        else
          echo "error: $bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal" >&2
          exit 1
        fi ;;
      --whole-build-plan)
        [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { echo "usage: $0 --whole-build-plan WORKERS [REPO_ROOT]" >&2; exit 2; }
        if bootstrap_tree_rss_whole_build_plan "$2" "${3:-}"; then
          printf 'workers=%s\ncap_kib=%s\nceiling_kib=%s\nbudget_kib=%s\nbound=%s\ncli_row_cap_kib=%s\ncli_row_ceiling_kib=%s\ncli_row_bound=%s\nhost_total_kib=%s\nhost_available_kib=%s\nhost_total_source=%s\nsummary=%s\n' \
            "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_workers" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cap_kib" \
            "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_ceiling_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_budget_kib" \
            "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_bound" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_cap_kib" \
            "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_ceiling_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_cli_row_bound" \
            "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_kib" \
            "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_available_kib" "$bootstrap_tree_rss_host_total_source" \
            "$bootstrap_tree_rss_plan_summary"
        else
          echo "error: $bootstrap_tree_rss_refusal" >&2
          exit 1
        fi ;;
      *) echo "usage: $0 --selftest | --resolve JOBS [REPO_ROOT] | --whole-build-plan WORKERS [REPO_ROOT]" >&2; exit 2 ;;
    esac ;;
esac
